```
id: SPL-002
name: Password spray against Windows or directory accounts
description: One source fails authentication against many distinct accounts with few attempts per
   account.
platform: Splunk
mitre_tactic: Credential Access
mitre_technique: T1110.003 Brute Force: Password Spraying
severity: High
data_source: index=wineventlog (Security)
false_positives: Corporate NAT egress after a password policy change; devices retrying with old
   credentials.
tuning: Maintain an exclusion lookup for trusted source ranges; tune distinct_users to
   environment size.
test_method: From one host, attempt a single wrong password against ten lab accounts.
owner: <OWNER>
status: Draft
last_review: 2026-11-19
```
index=wineventlog sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4625 earliest=-1h
| where isnotnull(src) AND src!="-"
| stats count AS attempts dc(user) AS distinct_users values(user) AS user_sample min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY src
| eval avg_attempts_per_user=round(attempts/distinct_users,1)
| where distinct_users>=10 AND avg_attempts_per_user<=3
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort - distinct_users
